-- created : 2026-09-27T02:58:16.670522+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/18b0b75a-13d7-42cd-b397-d2a86dcffae6
-- title:
--   Fixed rounded LP coefficient templates
-- statement:
--   This bundle fixes an ordered array called roundedTemplates containing $1{,}525$ row-template records, by appending $61$ private literal arrays numbered $0$ through $60$, each with $25$ records. A record has a finite Unicode name string, a Boolean standard-only flag, a natural precision, an index-pool tag, an ordered list of integer-coefficient/feature pairs, and an integer right-hand side. Pool tags select nodes, darts, faces, outgoing darts at nodes, or darts of a specified face size. Features are syntactic requests for a node, dart or face coordinate, or a list of node or dart coordinates, at an address formed from bound objects, all nodes, next/previous/reversed darts, the initial node of a dart, the first member of a dart list, or the containing face. The fixed data have $1{,}085$ false-flag records and $440$ true-flag records, all with precision in $\{3,4,5,6,7\}$; all $1{,}525$ triples (name, flag, precision) are distinct. The integer coefficients and right-hand sides are literal stored values; this declaration computes no numerical rounding operation and supplies no proof of their geometric inequalities. For an arbitrary Boolean $s$, natural precision $p$ and string $n$, lookup first searches for the earliest record whose name equals $n$, precision equals $p$, and flag equals true if $s$ is true; if that search fails, it searches for the earliest corresponding false-flag record. When $s$ is false it searches only false-flag records. Equality tests are exact and a failed search returns no record. There is no separate range condition on the lookup arguments; for example any precision outside $\{3,4,5,6,7\}$ has no match. Empty names and arbitrary strings are permitted lookup inputs. Array order is preserved, and these definitions assert no decoding success, feasibility, infeasibility, certificate existence or soundness.
--
--   **Source and scope.** Primary §9; formal_lp/hypermap/ineqs/lp_ineqs.hl:265–320, lp_approx_ineqs.hl:106–216, constants_approx.hl. All 1,525 fixed integer templates preserve source outward rounding and precisions 3–7.
-- source:
